course: dictionary
lesson: 5810
title: Maglev: trains that float
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A maglev is a train that floats just above its track, so it never touches the rails. The name is short for «magnetic levitation»: magnetic means it uses magnets, and levitation means rising up into the air without touching anything.
explain: In science you learn that like poles of magnets push apart. Maglev trains use powerful magnets like this to push the train up off the track, so it floats.
explain: «Maglev trains use strong magnets to float above the track and move along it; with no wheels touching, there is almost no friction.» Friction is the rubbing that slows things down. Less friction means a smoother, faster ride.
fact: Maglev is short for «magnetic levitation».
fact: A «maglev» means a train that floats above its track using magnets.
fact: Maglev trains run in China and Japan.
fact: «Friction» means the rubbing that slows things down.
fact: Like poles of magnets push apart, and this push is what lifts a maglev train.
exercise: What does «maglev» mean? | A bicycle with magnets in the wheels | A bus that runs on electric wires | *A train that floats above its track using magnets | A boat that sails under the sea
exercise: Maglev is short for «magnetic levitation». What does levitation mean? | Sinking to the bottom of a lake | Digging a tunnel under the ground | *Floating up into the air without touching anything | Spinning very fast on one wheel
exercise: «With no wheels touching, there is almost no friction.» Why is there almost no friction on a maglev? | Because the train is very small | *Because no wheels touch the track | Because the track is wet | Because the train is painted green
test: Where do maglev trains run? | In a desert | In the Arctic | In a town in England | *In China and Japan
test: In «Maglev trains use strong magnets to float above the track», what does track mean? | A ticket for the train | *The rails the train runs along | A type of magnet | A song about trains
exam: What is a maglev? | *A train that floats above its track using magnets | A ship that sails on rivers | A plane that flies over the sea | A car that runs on petrol
